course: dictionary
lesson: 15010
title: What is left behind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A residue is the small amount that is left behind after the main part has gone or been used. «There was a sticky residue on the table after the jam jar was wiped.» The jam has gone, but a little sticky leftover stays. Residue is a noun, so you can say a residue or several residues.
explain: In science, residue is what remains after a process such as evaporating, burning or filtering. «When the salty water dried, a white residue was left in the dish.» The water went into the air, and the salt stayed behind. Look for clues like left, remains and stays behind.
explain: A good check is to swap in the words "what is left". «The filter paper had a brown residue on it.» That means "the brown part left on the filter paper", and the meaning still makes sense.
fact: Residue is a noun: a residue, residues.
fact: «Residue» means a small amount left behind after the main part has gone or been used.
fact: In a science lab, filtering can leave a residue on the filter paper, and burning leaves ash.
fact: Pesticide residue is a tiny amount of chemical left on fruit, which is why we wash fruit well.
fact: In advanced maths, the residue is the remainder left over after dividing.
exercise: «After the water boiled away, a white residue was left in the pan.» What is the white residue? | A new kind of water | The pan itself | The steam that rose up into the kitchen | *The small amount left behind after the water went
exercise: Sam says residue means the main part of something. What does residue really mean? | *A small amount left behind after the main part has gone | A sticky sweet | The main part that stays whole | A kind of bottle
exercise: Which word is a good swap for residue in «a sticky residue on the table»? | a sticky sweet | a sticky friend | *a sticky leftover | a sticky dance
test: «Burning the paper left only a little grey ash, the residue.» What does residue mean here? | *What is left after burning | The paper before it burned | The smoke that floated away | The flames that danced up
test: In advanced maths, 17 divided by 5 is 3 with 2 left over. What is the residue? | 3 | *2 | 17 | 5
exam: Which sentence uses residue correctly? | *After the puddle dried, a thin residue of mud was left on the path | The residue ran fast across the field | The bird sang a residue of songs | I ate a residue for lunch
